# Pramniaga Frontend React

Follow [`.cursor/CODE_STANDARDS.md`](../CODE_STANDARDS.md) and [`.cursor/FILE_STRUCTURE.md`](../FILE_STRUCTURE.md).

## Placement

- Primitives → `components/ui/` + barrel `index.ts` (`@/components/ui`). Until split, keep adding to `ui.tsx` only for tiny one-offs; prefer extracting when the file grows.
- Chrome → `components/layout/`. Domain widgets → `components/<domain>/`. Screens → `pages/<domain>/`.
- Shared non-UI → `lib/` (`api.ts` is the JSDoc gold standard).

## Docs & naming

- File header: Purpose, Exports, Last updated, Author: Pramniaga.
- Every exported function/component/default page export:

```
Name - Description.

@param ...
@returns ...
```

- Variables: `camelCase`, intent-first (`overviewCounts`, `showForm`). Booleans: `is`/`has`/`can`/`show`.
- No narrating `//` that only repeats the next statement.
- Method strings only in `lib/api.ts`. Cover loading / empty / error UI states.
- Auth: keep protected UI gated until session refresh completes; do not trust boot session alone.

## Colors (design tokens)

Tokens live in `frontend/src/index.css` (`:root` RGB channels) and are wired in `tailwind.config.js`. Prefer token utilities over raw hex.

| Token | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `brand` / `brand-dark` | Primary actions, active nav, brand accents |
| `canvas` | Page / shell background (frosted chrome uses `rgb(var(--canvas) / α)`) |
| `surface-2` | Subtle fills (inputs, idle hovers that are not semantic) |
| `ink` / `ink-muted` | Body text / secondary text |
| `line` | Borders, hairlines |
| `danger` | Destructive actions (logout, delete) |
| `accent` | Occasional highlight only — not a second brand |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — one-off hex / gray stacks
className="bg-[#F3F3F3] text-gray-500 hover:bg-gray-100"

// ✅ GOOD — tokens + alpha when needed
className="bg-canvas text-ink-muted hover:bg-brand/10 hover:text-brand"
className="hover:bg-danger/10 hover:text-danger" // logout / destructive
```

- Soft hovers: tint with `/10` (or similar), do not slam full `bg-surface-2` on destructive/logout.
- Frosted chrome (e.g. topbar): base = canvas + alpha + `backdrop-filter`; domain class `shell-topbar` / `shell-topbar--scrolled`.
- New colors: add `--token` in `:root`, map in Tailwind, then use utilities — do not sprinkle hex in components.

## Icon hover (shake)

Shared motion lives in `index.css` as `.icon-shake` under a parent `.group`. **Any labeled icon button should shake its icon on hover** (Back, Preview, Edit, nav, logout, etc.) — not only sidebar chrome.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — parent is group; icon gets icon-shake
<Button type="button" variant="secondary" className="group" onClick={…}>
  <Eye className="icon-shake h-4 w-4" />
  Preview
</Button>

<button className="group … hover:bg-danger/10 hover:text-danger">
  <LogOut className="icon-shake h-4 w-4" />
</button>

<a className="group …">
  <span className="…"><Icon className="icon-shake h-3.5 w-3.5" /></span>
  Label
</a>
```

- Parent control must include `group`; the icon (or logo `<img>`) gets `icon-shake`.
- Do not invent a second shake keyframe; respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (already gated in CSS).
- Pair distinct icons with distinct actions (e.g. `Eye` = Preview, `Pencil` = Edit, `ArrowLeft` = Back) — do not reuse the same glyph for both Preview and Edit.
- Hover background is separate: pick a token tint that matches intent (danger for logout, `brand/10` or `surface-2` for nav).

## CSS / classes

- Prefer tokens above over raw hex.
- Custom classes: `domain-role` (`login-brand-mesh`, `shell-topbar`, `icon-shake`). Exported style strings: `*Class` by role (`pillInputClass`).
- Labels must match data (`To process` only for draft queues; totals say `Active`/`Total`).
